{"_v":1,"id":"spring-awakening-2006","bd":{"positive":5,"mixed":0,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2006/legit/reviews/spring-awakening-1200516066/","d":"2006-12-11","q":"This strange, beguiling show is by no means flawless, but with subtle, nurturing changes, the creative team and cast have fashioned an already seductive work into something even more lovely and lyrical."},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/lifestyle/2006/12/11/spring-awakening-blooms-on-broadway/","d":"2006-12-11","q":"Spring Awakening is a musical of exceptional power and beauty, a show that succeeds in making the late 19th century feel urgently contemporary."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":81,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2006/12/11/theater/reviews/11spri.html","d":"2006-12-11","q":"This agonizing state may not sound like something you want to return to, but “Spring Awakening” has been created with such care and craft that the voyage back is a deeply rewarding one."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Newsday","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.newsday.com/entertainment/theater/spring-awakening-review-deaf-culture-in-a-revelatory-rock-musical-1.10890858","q":"The results are moving and both visually and musically impressive, if ultimately a bit repetitious."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/spring-awakening/","d":"2009-01-31","q":"Bravo, the evening is a calculated risk for everyone involved and the results are seductively mesmerizing."}],"au":{"score":92,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"ss":{"s":92,"c":550},"mz":{"s":91,"c":528,"sr":4.6}}},"hi":"/images/shows/spring-awakening-2006/hero.webp","ta":"230 W 49th St, New York, NY 10019","pd":"2006-11-16","ca":[{"n":"Skylar Astin","r":"Georg"},{"n":"Gerard Canonico","r":"Ensemble"},{"n":"Lilli Cooper","r"